<section class="page-hero practice-page-hero"><div class="container page-hero-grid"><div class="reveal"><div class="eyebrow">Practice Area · 03 · Intellectual Property</div><h1>Trademark Infringement / Passing</h1><p>Protection of brands, trademarks, names and goodwill against misuse, infringement and passing off.</p><a class="btn btn-gold" href="<?= site_url('appointment') ?>">Request Appointment ↗</a></div><div class="page-art glass-card reveal"><img class="practice-page-image" src="<?= base_url('assets/practice-art/trademark-infringement.png') ?>" alt="Intellectual Property legal illustration" /></div></div><div class="orb main" data-depth=".55"></div><div class="orbit" data-depth=".85"></div></section>
<section class="section light"><div class="container matter-rich"><div class="matter-rich-main reveal"><div class="eyebrow">Overview</div><h2>Clear advice begins with a clear factual picture.</h2><p class="lead-dark">A brand dispute may turn on the marks involved, the goods or services, the market in which they are used and the evidence of confusion or misuse. Early preservation of records and a clear assessment of the commercial position can be important. The information below is intended to help a visitor understand the kinds of questions commonly discussed and the documents that may be useful for an initial review.</p><div class="context-grid"><div class="glass-light reveal"><span>01</span><h3>Pre-action infringement assessment</h3><p>Brand disputes can require a close comparison of marks, goods or services, market context and the evidence of actual or likely confusion.</p></div><div class="glass-light reveal"><span>02</span><h3>Cease-and-desist strategy</h3><p>Early action may include preserving evidence, assessing the strength of rights and choosing a proportionate response.</p></div><div class="glass-light reveal"><span>03</span><h3>Trademark and brand portfolio review</h3><p>For contested matters, strategy can include interim protection, pleadings, evidence and coordination around commercial continuity.</p></div><div class="glass-light reveal"><span>04</span><h3>Civil remedies and injunction strategy</h3><p>For contested matters, strategy can include interim protection, pleadings, evidence and coordination around commercial continuity.</p></div></div></div><aside class="matter-quote glass-light reveal"><span class="smallcaps">LEX FACTUM / 03</span><blockquote>“The right next step starts with understanding the right facts.”</blockquote><p>Specific legal outcomes depend on the facts, evidence, procedure and applicable law. This page is informational and not legal advice.</p></aside></div></section>
<section class="section dark"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow">How a matter is approached</div><h2>A practical, structured view.</h2></div></div><div class="detail-grid"><div class="detail-block reveal"><span class="eyebrow">01 / Context</span><h3>Understanding the matter</h3><p>Brand disputes can require a close comparison of marks, goods or services, market context and the evidence of actual or likely confusion.</p></div><div class="detail-block reveal"><span class="eyebrow">02 / Context</span><h3>Preparing the record</h3><p>Early action may include preserving evidence, assessing the strength of rights and choosing a proportionate response.</p></div><div class="detail-block reveal"><span class="eyebrow">03 / Context</span><h3>Choosing the next step</h3><p>For contested matters, strategy can include interim protection, pleadings, evidence and coordination around commercial continuity.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section practice-intro-dark"><div class="container feature-practice"><div class="feature-copy reveal"><div class="eyebrow">Related considerations</div><h2>Preparation matters as much as presentation.</h2><p>For an initial discussion, it can help to bring relevant notices, orders, agreements, correspondence, identification documents and a simple chronology of key events, where applicable.</p></div><div class="feature-art glass-card reveal"><img class="practice-feature-image" src="<?= base_url('assets/practice-art/trademark-infringement.png') ?>" alt="Intellectual Property legal illustration" /></div></div></section>
